  "opengs_title": "Procedural Generation (Open-Source)",
  "opengs_desc": "💡 Supporting Open-Source: We love open-source! We highly recommend and support the amazing 'opengs-maptool' created by Thomas Holtvedt. We recognize a great idea when we see one!\n\n🎯 Division of Roles: Our focus is delivering the smoothest map editor possible, while opengs-maptool shines in procedural generation. Everyone doing what they do best! haha.\n\n⚠️ The Python Drama: To run the generator directly here, we'd have to execute Python dynamically. Unlike Lua (which is super lightweight in Dart), Python requires dragging a huge 'elephant' of dependencies that would make our app heavily bloated and slow!\n\n🛠️ Avoiding Outdated Code: Rewriting his logic into our code would be a terrible architectural choice. We'd fall behind quickly while the creator keeps updating his tool.\n\n🤝 The Smart Choice: Directing you to the author's repo (giving proper credit) and just importing the final file is the lightest, most honest, and practical solution!",
